- Intermediate
- Contains-Eggs
- Vegetarian
title: Spanish Omelette
method: stovetop
source: https://www.thespanishchef.com/recipes/tortilla-de-patatas
protein: eggs
ingredient_count: 4
---

Begin by peeling and slicing the @waxy potatoes{3%medium}(peeled and halved) into thin, uniform rounds (about 3mm thick). This consistency is crucial for even cooking.

Heat the @olive oil{400%ml} in a #non-stick pan{} over medium heat. The oil should be abundant enough to almost cover the potatoes.

Add the sliced potatoes to the oil, and if using onion, add @Spanish onion{1}(peeled and finely chopped) as well. Cook slowly, stirring occasionally, until the potatoes are tender but not browned (about ~{15-20%minutes}).

Meanwhile, crack the @eggs{8} into a #large bowl{} and beat them well. Season with @salt.

Once the potatoes are tender, drain them through a #colander{}, reserving a small amount of oil for cooking the tortilla.

Add the warm potato-onion mixture to the beaten eggs, gently stirring to combine. Let the mixture rest for ~{5%minutes} to allow the flavours to meld.

Heat 2 tablespoons of the reserved oil in your non-stick pan over medium heat.

Pour in the egg-potato mixture, shaking the pan gently to ensure even distribution. Cook for about ~{4-5%minutes} until the bottom is golden but the top is still slightly runny.

Place a #large plate{} over the non-stick pan and, in one confident motion, turn the tortilla onto the #plate{}.

Slide the tortilla back into the non-stick pan, uncooked side down, and cook for another ~{3-4%minutes} until golden.